    <DataNode elementId="AT3G47450-MONOMER" textLabel="NO-associated protein 1, chloroplastic/mitochondrial" type="Protein">
      <Xref identifier="Q66GP9" dataSource="uniprot" />
      <Graphics centerX="150" centerY="215" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="000000" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="000000" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment source="pmngroup">This protein was originally believed to function as a nitric oxide synthase (AtNOS1) |CITS: [14526079]|. However, later work has shown that this enzyme functions as a GTPase |CITS: [18801746]|. Further investigation will be required to understand NO biosynthesis in Arabidopsis. NO deficient plants show inhibited plant growth, less fertility, abnormal stomatal movement and changed hormone signaling indicating the vital role of this enzyme |CITS:[14526079]|. However, other groups could not find NOS activity in Arabidopsis suggesting that further research is needed |CITS:[17030145]|.</Comment>
      <Property key="UniqueID" value="AT3G47450-MONOMER" />
