      <Comment source="THE-ARABIDOPSIS-INFORMATION-RESOURCE, hartmut">The enzymatic activity reversibly converting argininosuccinate to arginine and fumarate, i.e. argininosuccinate lyase (EC 4.3.2.1) has been identified and partially purified from leaves of &lt;i&gt;Arabidopsis thaliana&lt;/i&gt;. It has been established that the enzyme is dependent on fumarate and that the forward reaction is favored forming arginine and fumarate |CITS:[17651442]|.</Comment>
