      <Graphics centerX="500" centerY="680" width="90.0" height="25.0" textColor="3955e7" fontName="Arial" fontWeight="Normal" fontStyle="Normal" fontDecoration="Normal" fontStrikethru="Normal" fontSize="12" hAlign="Center" vAlign="Middle" borderColor="3955e7" borderStyle="Solid" borderWidth="1.0" fillColor="FFFFFF" shapeType="Rectangle" />
      <Comment>|FRAME: L-CITRULLINE| is a non-standard amino acid that is not normally incorporated into proteins during protein synthesis. Citrulline was first isolated from |FRAME:TAX-3653| (watermelon) in 1914 |CITS: [Koga14]|. It was re-isolated in 1930, at which time its chemical formula was determined and it was named (after the Latin name of the watermelon) |CITS: [Wada30]|.</Comment>
